{%- comment -%}
  Virtual Try-On modal.
  Rendered once, globally, from layout/theme.liquid on product pages only.
  All interactivity lives in assets/vto.js.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div id="VtoModal" class="vto-modal" role="dialog" aria-modal="true"
     aria-label="Virtual Try-On" hidden>
  <div class="vto-modal__overlay" data-vto-close></div>
  <div class="vto-modal__container" tabindex="-1">

    {%- comment -%} Drag handle (mobile bottom sheet). Active — not decorative. {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="vto-drag-handle" data-vto-drag-handle aria-hidden="true"></div>

    {%- comment -%} Header {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="vto-modal__header">
      <button type="button" class="vto-modal__back" data-vto-back aria-label="Go back" hidden>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
          <polyline points="15 18 9 12 15 6"/>
        </svg>
      </button>
      <div class="vto-modal__header-left">
        <div class="vto-modal__logo" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M20.38 3.46L16 2a4 4 0 0 1-8 0L3.62 3.46a2 2 0 0 0-1.34 2.23l.58 3.57a1 1 0 0 0 .99.84H6v10c0 1.1.9 2 2 2h8a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V10h2.15a1 1 0 0 0 .99-.84l.58-3.57a2 2 0 0 0-1.34-2.23z"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h2 class="vto-modal__title">Virtual Try-On</h2>
      </div>
      <button type="button" class="vto-modal__close" data-vto-close
              aria-label="Close virtual try-on">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
          <line x1="18" y1="6" x2="6" y2="18"/>
          <line x1="6" y1="6" x2="18" y2="18"/>
        </svg>
      </button>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      The live region used to sit here, inside #VtoModal. minimize() ends with
      `modal.hidden = true`, and a hidden subtree is out of the accessibility
      tree entirely — so every announcement made while minimised ("still
      creating your look", "your look is ready") was written into a node no
      screen reader could see. The floating pill's own role="status" was
      covering for that, and the pill is gone. It now lives at the end of this
      file, as a sibling of the modal, where it is never hidden.
    {%- endcomment -%}

    {%- comment -%} ─── Screen 1: Upload ──────────────────────── {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="vto-screen" data-vto-screen="upload">

      {%- comment -%}
        Consent gate. Camera and Library stay disabled until this is ticked —
        assets/vto.js enforces it on the controls AND on the drop zone, so a
        drag-and-drop cannot walk around the checkbox.

        Deliberately not pre-ticked, and the label names what is being agreed to
        rather than pointing vaguely at a policy page.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="vto-consent" data-vto-consent-wrap>
        <input type="checkbox" id="VtoConsent" data-vto-consent>
        <label for="VtoConsent">
          <b>I agree to the Privacy Policy</b>
          It covers how your photo is processed, and that OnRepeat may use your photo and the look it generates for creative purposes. You can opt out any time through <a href="/pages/contact" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Contact&nbsp;us</a>.
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="vto-upload-area" data-vto-dropzone>
        <div class="vto-upload-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M20 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H8a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/>
            <circle cx="12" cy="7" r="4"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <p class="vto-upload-text">Add your photo</p>
        <p class="vto-upload-hint">One full-body shot, facing the camera.</p>
        <input type="file" accept="image/jpeg,image/png,image/webp,image/heic,image/heif"
               class="vto-file-input" data-vto-file-input aria-label="Choose photo" />
        <div class="vto-upload-actions">
          <button type="button" class="vto-btn-primary vto-upload-btn">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"/>
              <polyline points="17 8 12 3 7 8"/>
              <line x1="12" y1="3" x2="12" y2="15"/>
            </svg>
            Library
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="vto-btn-ghost vto-camera-btn" data-vto-camera>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M14.5 4h-5L7 7H4a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2h-3l-2.5-3z"/>
              <circle cx="12" cy="13" r="3"/>
            </svg>
            Camera
          </button>
        </div>
        <p class="vto-upload-lock" data-vto-upload-lock>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="11" rx="2"/><path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4"/>
          </svg>
          Agree above to add a photo
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="vto-privacy-notice">
        Your photo is sent to Google, or to OpenAI if Google is unavailable, to generate the try-on. Read the full <a href="/policies/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </div>

      <div class="vto-tips" data-vto-tips>
        <span class="vto-tip"><span class="vto-tip__icon">✓</span> Stand straight, arms slightly apart</span>
        <span class="vto-tip"><span class="vto-tip__icon">✓</span> Bright, even lighting</span>
        <span class="vto-tip"><span class="vto-tip__icon">✓</span> Full body visible</span>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} Recent try-ons (populated from sessionStorage) {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="vto-recent" data-vto-recent hidden>
        <div class="vto-recent__label">Recent try-ons</div>
        <div class="vto-recent__list" data-vto-recent-list></div>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} Preview after photo selection {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="vto-preview" data-vto-preview hidden>
        <div class="vto-preview__photo-wrap">
          <img alt="Your uploaded photo" data-vto-preview-img />
          <div class="vto-preview__badge">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/>
            </svg>
            Photo ready
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="vto-preview-actions">
          <button type="button" class="vto-btn-ghost" data-vto-change-photo>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <polyline points="1 4 1 10 7 10"/><polyline points="23 20 23 14 17 14"/>
              <path d="M20.49 9A9 9 0 0 0 5.64 5.64L1 10m22 4-4.64 4.36A9 9 0 0 1 3.51 15"/>
            </svg>
            Change
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="vto-btn-primary" data-vto-generate>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <polygon points="5 3 19 12 5 21 5 3"/>
            </svg>
            Try It On
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} ─── Screen 2: Fit ────────────────────────────
      Required. The ease, tone and build have to exist BEFORE the generation
      request goes out, or the model cannot cut the garment to this body — which
      is the whole reason this step is not optional and carries no skip.

      The questions, the slider ranges and the answer all come from the size
      guide's own engine (window.OnRepeatSizeChart) so the modal and the product
      page cannot disagree about a shopper's size.
    ─────────────────────────────────────────────── {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%} ─── Screen 2a: Confirm saved measurements ───────
      Shown on every try-on once measurements exist. They used to be reused
      silently forever, which is wrong in both directions: a shopper whose body
      has changed had no way to correct it short of clearing site data, and a
      shopper trying something on for someone else was silently given their own
      numbers. Neither had any way to know which measurements the render used.

      It stays one tap for the common case — "Yes, use these" is the primary
      action and is pre-focused — but the numbers are on screen first, and the
      size they imply for THIS product is spelled out, so the choice is
      informed rather than a formality.
    ─────────────────────────────────────────────── {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="vto-screen" data-vto-screen="fitconfirm" hidden>
      <div class="vto-fit vto-fitconfirm">
        <p class="vto-fit__kicker">Still the same measurements?</p>

        <div class="vto-fitconfirm__card">
          <dl class="vto-fitconfirm__grid">
            <div>
              <dt>Height</dt>
              <dd data-vto-confirm="height">175<small>cm</small></dd>
              <span class="vto-fitconfirm__alt" data-vto-confirm="heightAlt">5'9"</span>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Weight</dt>
              <dd data-vto-confirm="weight">70<small>kg</small></dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Build</dt>
              <dd data-vto-confirm="build">Average</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
          {%- comment -%}
            The consequence, not just the inputs. "178cm, 72kg" means nothing to
            most people; "we'll cut this to an M" is the thing they can actually
            check. Hidden when the product has no solvable chart.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <p class="vto-fitconfirm__size" data-vto-confirm-size hidden></p>
        </div>

        <div class="vto-fitconfirm__actions">
          <button type="button" class="vto-btn-primary" data-vto-confirm-keep>Yes, use these</button>
          <button type="button" class="vto-btn-ghost" data-vto-confirm-edit>Enter new measurements</button>
        </div>

        <p class="vto-fit__note">Measurements stay on your device. Change them any time from here.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="vto-screen" data-vto-screen="fit" hidden>
      <div class="vto-fit">
        <div class="vto-fit__dots" data-vto-fit-dots aria-hidden="true">
          <i class="is-on"></i><i></i><i></i>
        </div>
        <p class="vto-fit__kicker" data-vto-fit-kicker>Three questions. Answered once, and every try-on after this one is cut to them.</p>

        <div class="vto-fit__step" data-vto-fit-step="1">
          <p class="vto-fit__q" id="VtoFitQ1">How tall are you, without shoes?</p>
          <p class="vto-fit__sub">In centimetres</p>
          <p class="vto-fit__val">
            <b data-vto-fit-out="height">175</b><small>cm</small>
            <span class="vto-fit__alt" data-vto-fit-out="heightAlt">5'9"</span>
          </p>
          <input class="vto-fit__range" type="range" min="140" max="210" step="1" value="175"
                 data-vto-fit-in="height" aria-labelledby="VtoFitQ1">
        </div>

        <div class="vto-fit__step" data-vto-fit-step="2" hidden>
          <p class="vto-fit__q" id="VtoFitQ2">And roughly what do you weigh?</p>
          <p class="vto-fit__sub">In kilograms</p>
          <p class="vto-fit__val"><b data-vto-fit-out="weight">70</b><small>kg</small></p>
          <input class="vto-fit__range" type="range" min="35" max="150" step="1" value="70"
                 data-vto-fit-in="weight" aria-labelledby="VtoFitQ2">
        </div>

        <div class="vto-fit__step" data-vto-fit-step="3" hidden>
          <p class="vto-fit__q" id="VtoFitQ3">How would you describe your build?</p>
          <p class="vto-fit__sub" data-vto-fit-noun>This fine-tunes the chest estimate</p>
          <p class="vto-fit__val vto-fit__val--word"><b data-vto-fit-out="build">Average</b></p>
          {%- comment -%}
            A slider whose values are words, so a screen reader reads the label
            rather than the index behind it.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <input class="vto-fit__range" type="range" min="0" max="3" step="1" value="1"
                 data-vto-fit-in="build" aria-labelledby="VtoFitQ3" aria-valuetext="Average">
        </div>

        <div class="vto-fit__actions">
          <button type="button" class="vto-btn-ghost" data-vto-fit-back hidden>Back</button>
          <button type="button" class="vto-btn-primary" data-vto-fit-next>Next</button>
        </div>

        <p class="vto-fit__note">We use this to size the render, and to tell you which size to pick. It stays on your device.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} ─── Screen 3: Loading ─────────────────────── {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="vto-screen" data-vto-screen="loading" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden>
      <div class="vto-loading">
        <div class="vto-loading-illustration" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="vto-scan-container">
            <!-- 1. Garment silhouette vector -->
            <svg class="vto-scan-svg vto-scan-svg--garment" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2">
              <path d="M20.38 3.46L16 2a4 4 0 0 1-8 0L3.62 3.46a2 2 0 0 0-1.34 2.23l.58 3.57a1 1 0 0 0 .99.84H6v10c0 1.1.9 2 2 2h8a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V10h2.15a1 1 0 0 0 .99-.84l.58-3.57a2 2 0 0 0-1.34-2.23z"/>
            </svg>
            <!-- 2. Avatar silhouette vector -->
            <svg class="vto-scan-svg vto-scan-svg--avatar" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2">
              <path d="M20 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H8a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/>
              <circle cx="12" cy="7" r="4"/>
            </svg>
            <!-- 3. Glowing laser bar -->
            <div class="vto-scan-laser"></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="vto-loading-title" data-vto-loading-title>Creating your look</p>

        <div class="vto-steps">
          <div class="vto-step" data-vto-step="1">
            <div class="vto-step__dot" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            <span class="vto-step__label">Analyzing your photo</span>
          </div>
          <div class="vto-step" data-vto-step="2">
            <div class="vto-step__dot" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            <span class="vto-step__label">Reading the garment</span>
          </div>
          <div class="vto-step" data-vto-step="3">
            <div class="vto-step__dot" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            <span class="vto-step__label">Generating your look</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="vto-loading-elapsed">
          <span class="vto-loading-elapsed__time" data-vto-elapsed role="timer" aria-label="Time elapsed">0s</span>
          <span class="vto-loading-elapsed__sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          {%- comment -%}
            Re-measured against gemini-3.1-flash-image at thinkingLevel MINIMAL:
            14.8s of model time, 17-19s end to end, across live runs on the
            deployed function. The old "60-90s" was measured against
            gpt-image-2 (front 46-53s, back 50-79s) and now understates the
            product badly — a shopper told to expect 90s abandons a 20s wait.
            The upper bound leaves room for a cold start and for the back view,
            which runs in parallel so the wait tracks the slower of the two.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <span class="vto-loading-elapsed__note" data-vto-elapsed-note>usually 20&ndash;45s</span>
        </p>

        {%- comment -%} ─── Recent looks ───────────────────────────
          Something to watch while the render runs. The images are seeded
          try-ons generated with the SAME prompt and model the shopper is
          waiting on, so the strip is an honest sample of what is coming
          rather than nicer marketing art.

          Deliberately NOT captioned as other customers' try-ons: these are
          made from the store's own catalogue photography, and claiming
          otherwise would be a straightforward lie to the shopper. Real
          customer looks need storage, consent and moderation first.

          The list is rendered as JSON and shuffled on the client. Liquid
          output is cached per theme version, so shuffling here would hand
          every shopper the same "random" order.
        ─────────────────────────────────────────────── {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign gallery_count = 20 -%}
        <div class="vto-gallery" data-vto-gallery hidden>
          <p class="vto-gallery__label">Recent looks, made with this try-on</p>
          <div class="vto-gallery__viewport">
            <div class="vto-gallery__track" data-vto-gallery-track aria-hidden="true"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <script type="application/json" data-vto-gallery-src>
          [
            {%- for i in (1..gallery_count) -%}
              {%- assign padded = i | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2 -%}
              {%- assign file = 'vto-gallery-' | append: padded | append: '-thumb.webp' -%}
              "{{ file | asset_url }}"{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          ]
        </script>

        {%- comment -%}
          translate="no" keeps browser and app translation engines off this node.
          It is rewritten every few seconds from JS, and a foreign mutator racing
          those writes produced garbled overlapping text in testing (including a
          stray glyph belonging to no string this file contains).
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <p class="vto-loading-hint" data-vto-loading-hint translate="no">You can keep browsing — we'll let you know the moment it's ready.</p>

        <div class="vto-loading-actions">
          <button type="button" class="vto-btn-primary vto-minimize-btn" data-vto-minimize>
            {%- comment -%}
              Was a single horizontal line, which next to the label read as a
              stray hyphen. A chevron down into a bar says "tuck this away".
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <polyline points="7 9 12 14 17 9"/>
              <line x1="5" y1="19" x2="19" y2="19"/>
            </svg>
            Keep browsing
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="vto-btn-ghost vto-cancel-btn" data-vto-cancel>
            Cancel
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} ─── Screen 3: Results ─────────────────────── {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%} ─── Screen 3: Results ───────────────────────
      The buy block is PINNED. It used to sit below a 3:4 image in a scrolling
      screen, which on a phone put the size rail and Add to Cart entirely below
      the fold — a shopper reached the end of the flow and saw no way to buy.
      The image now takes whatever height is left over instead of dictating it.

      Front/Back and the save/share tools sit ON the image as controls rather
      than as rows above and below it, so they cost the result no height.
    ─────────────────────────────────────────────── {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="vto-screen vto-screen--results" data-vto-screen="results" hidden>
      <div class="vto-results">

        <div class="vto-results__stage">
          <div class="vto-results__image" data-vto-result-wrap>
            <img class="vto-results__after" src="" alt="Virtual try-on result" data-vto-result-img />
            <div class="vto-results__shimmer" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          </div>

          <div class="vto-results__controls">
          <div class="vto-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Try-on view">
            <div class="vto-tabs__indicator" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            <button type="button" class="vto-tab active" role="tab" data-vto-tab="front" aria-selected="true">Front</button>
            <button type="button" class="vto-tab" role="tab" data-vto-tab="back" aria-selected="false" data-vto-back-tab>Back</button>
          </div>
          </div>

          <div class="vto-results__tools">
            <button type="button" data-vto-download aria-label="Save this image">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"/>
                <polyline points="7 10 12 15 17 10"/>
                <line x1="12" y1="15" x2="12" y2="3"/>
              </svg>
            </button>
            <button type="button" data-vto-share aria-label="Share this image">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <circle cx="18" cy="5" r="3"/><circle cx="6" cy="12" r="3"/><circle cx="18" cy="19" r="3"/>
                <line x1="8.59" y1="13.51" x2="15.42" y2="17.49"/>
                <line x1="15.41" y1="6.51" x2="8.59" y2="10.49"/>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="vto-results__buy">
        <div class="vto-verdict" data-vto-verdict hidden>
          <span class="vto-verdict__badge" data-vto-verdict-size>M</span>
          <span class="vto-verdict__txt">
            <span class="vto-verdict__lead">
              Your size
              <span class="vto-verdict__chip" data-vto-verdict-tone></span>
            </span>
            <span class="vto-verdict__why" data-vto-verdict-why></span>
          </span>
        </div>

          <div class="vto-buy-bar" data-vto-buy-bar>
          <div class="vto-size" data-vto-size-wrap>
            <div class="vto-size__head">
              <span class="vto-size__label">Size</span>
            </div>
            <div class="vto-size__pills" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Select size" data-vto-size-pills></div>
            {%- comment -%}
              Once the shopper has answered the fit questions the rail collapses
              to the one size we are suggesting, and this is the way back to
              the rest. Rendered here rather than injected by the rail builder
              so it survives every rebuild of the pills, and hidden until there
              is actually something collapsed to reveal.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <button type="button" class="vto-size__change" data-vto-size-change hidden>Change size</button>
          </div>
          <button type="button" class="vto-btn-primary vto-atc-btn" data-vto-atc>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <circle cx="9" cy="21" r="1"/>
              <circle cx="20" cy="21" r="1"/>
              <path d="M1 1h4l2.68 13.39a2 2 0 0 0 2 1.61h9.72a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.61L23 6H6"/>
            </svg>
            <span data-vto-atc-label>Add to Cart</span>
          </button>
          </div>

        <div class="vto-reason" data-vto-reason hidden>
          <p class="vto-reason__q">Thanks &mdash; what was off?</p>
          <div class="vto-reason__row" role="group" aria-label="What was wrong">
            <button type="button" data-vto-reason-btn="not_my_face">Not my face</button>
            <button type="button" data-vto-reason-btn="garment_wrong">Garment wrong</button>
            <button type="button" data-vto-reason-btn="fit_off">Fit looks off</button>
            <button type="button" data-vto-reason-btn="poor_quality">Poor quality</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="vto-feedback__thanks" data-vto-feedback-thanks hidden>Noted. We use this to tune the model, never to identify you.</p>

          <div class="vto-results__foot">
        <div class="vto-feedback" data-vto-feedback>
              <span class="vto-feedback__label">Does this look right?</span>
              <button type="button" class="vto-feedback__btn" data-vto-feedback-btn="up" aria-label="Yes, this looks right" aria-pressed="false">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3zM7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3"/>
                </svg>
              </button>
              <button type="button" class="vto-feedback__btn" data-vto-feedback-btn="down" aria-label="No, something is off" aria-pressed="false">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M10 15v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3l4-9V2H5.72a2 2 0 0 0-2 1.7l-1.38 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2.3zm7-13h2.67A2.31 2.31 0 0 1 22 4v7a2.31 2.31 0 0 1-2.33 2H17"/>
                </svg>
              </button>
            </div>
            <div class="vto-results__quiet">
            <button type="button" class="vto-size__chart" data-vto-size-chart hidden>Size guide</button>
            <button type="button" data-vto-retry>Try another photo</button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} ─── Screen 4: Error ───────────────────────── {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="vto-screen" data-vto-screen="error" role="status" aria-live="assertive" hidden>
      <div class="vto-error">
        <div class="vto-error__icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/>
            <line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"/>
            <line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <p class="vto-error-title">Something went wrong</p>
        <p class="vto-error-text" data-vto-error-msg>Please try again.</p>
        <button type="button" class="vto-btn-primary" data-vto-retry>Try Again</button>
        <button type="button" class="vto-btn-ghost" data-vto-change-photo>Change Photo</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} Toast (used by add-to-cart success etc.) {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Two icons, one shown at a time. The toast used to hard-code the tick, so a
      failure was announced with a green success check next to it.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="vto-toast" data-vto-toast hidden>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" data-vto-toast-icon="success">
        <polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/>
      </svg>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" data-vto-toast-icon="error" hidden>
        <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"/><line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"/>
      </svg>
      <span data-vto-toast-msg>Added to cart</span>
      <a href="/cart" class="vto-toast__link" data-vto-toast-link>View cart</a>
    </div>

  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Size chart sheet — sibling of the modal container so it layers ABOVE it
    (never behind). Content is fetched from the same /pages/size-chart source
    the product page's size guide uses. Driven by assets/vto.js.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="vto-sizechart" data-vto-sizechart hidden>
    <div class="vto-sizechart__overlay" data-vto-sizechart-close></div>
    <div class="vto-sizechart__sheet" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Size chart">
      <div class="vto-sizechart__head">
        <span class="vto-sizechart__title">Size chart</span>
        <button type="button" class="vto-sizechart__close" data-vto-sizechart-close aria-label="Close size chart">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <line x1="18" y1="6" x2="6" y2="18"/><line x1="6" y1="6" x2="18" y2="18"/>
          </svg>
        </button>
      </div>
      <div class="vto-sizechart__body" data-vto-sizechart-body>
        <div class="vto-sizechart__loading"><span class="vto-spinner"></span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
{%- comment -%}
  ── The minimised try-on ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
  There is no floating pill any more.

  A minimised try-on collapses onto the buy bar's own 48px product thumbnail
  (rendered by snippets/vto-button.liquid with placement 'tile') and lives
  there — one object, in a place the shopper already knows, instead of a
  second identical tile floating over the card and landing on "Size guide".

  Two consequences are deliberate:
    · On a page with no buy bar there is no indicator at all. The session
      still runs and still persists; it reappears on the next product page.
    · The tile's only action is reopening the modal. Cancel, retry and the
      elapsed counter live on the modal's own loading and error screens.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Live region for screen readers. A sibling of #VtoModal, never hidden, so
  progress announcements still reach a screen reader while the modal is
  minimised — see the note where this used to sit, inside the dialog.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="vto-sr-only" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" data-vto-announce></div>
